WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.213 --> 00:00:17.138
"I've decided to enjoy this drive," Anne said to Marilla on the way to Mrs.

2
00:00:17.198 --> 00:00:17.978
Spencer's house.

3
00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:22.780
"I've learned you can nearly always enjoy something if you try hard.

4
00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:25.682
I'm not going to think about going back to the orphanage.

5
00:00:26.242 --> 00:00:28.263
I'm just going to think about the drive.

6
00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:31.084
Oh look, there's a wild rose!"

7
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.341
she went on.

8
00:00:32.361 --> 00:00:34.042
"Isn't it lovely?

9
00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:36.865
Wouldn't it be nice if roses could talk?

10
00:00:37.485 --> 00:00:40.668
And isn't pink the most bewitching color in the world?

11
00:00:41.308 --> 00:00:43.030
I love it, but I can't wear it.

12
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.472
Redheaded people can't wear pink.

13
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:50.476
Do you know anybody whose hair color changed when they grew up?"

14
00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:53.498
"No," said Marilla wearily.

15
00:00:53.518 --> 00:00:56.841
"And I don't think your hair color will change either."

16
00:00:56.861 --> 00:01:00.004
"Well, that's another hope gone.

17
00:01:00.732 --> 00:01:03.373
My life is a graveyard of buried hopes.

18
00:01:04.093 --> 00:01:05.854
That's a sentence I read in a book once.

19
00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:09.235
I say it to comfort myself when I'm disappointed."

20
00:01:09.256 --> 00:01:11.116
"How does it comfort you?"

21
00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:12.777
asked Marilla, surprised.

22
00:01:12.797 --> 00:01:19.600
"Why, because it sounds so nice and romantic, as if I were a heroine in a book."

23
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:25.322
"If you're going to keep talking, you should tell me something about yourself," said Marilla.

24
00:01:25.342 --> 00:01:26.763
"Can I make it up?"

25
00:01:27.223 --> 00:01:27.823
Anne asked.

26
00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:30.184
"It'll be much more interesting."

27
00:01:30.832 --> 00:01:32.853
"No, I don't want any stories.

28
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.414
Just stick to the facts.

29
00:01:34.874 --> 00:01:36.895
Where were you born and how old are you?"

30
00:01:37.355 --> 00:01:38.515
asked Marilla sternly.

31
00:01:38.535 --> 00:01:44.698
"I was eleven last March," said Anne, "and I was born in Nova Scotia.

32
00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:48.240
My father and mother were both high school teachers.

33
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.801
They were very poor and lived in a tiny yellow house.

34
00:01:52.541 --> 00:01:53.662
I was born in that house.

35
00:01:54.342 --> 00:01:59.633
Mrs. Thomas said I was an ugly baby, scrawny and thin, but that my mother thought I was

36
00:01:59.713 --> 00:02:00.973
perfectly beautiful.

37
00:02:01.673 --> 00:02:04.435
She died of fever when I was only three months old.

38
00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:08.036
And soon after, my father died from fever too.

39
00:02:08.857 --> 00:02:11.618
So I was an orphan and nobody knew what to do with me.

40
00:02:12.218 --> 00:02:16.900
Father and Mother had both come from places far away and had no relatives around.

41
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.641
Finally Mrs.

42
00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:22.663
Thomas took me in, even though she was poor and her husband was a drunk.

43
00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.544
I lived with them until I was eight years old.

44
00:02:26.236 --> 00:02:29.217
I helped look after the children, and it was hard work.

45
00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:30.777
Then Mr.

46
00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.238
Thomas was killed when he fell under a train.

47
00:02:33.918 --> 00:02:36.759
After that I lived with the Hammonds, who had eight children.

48
00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:39.380
She had twins three times!

49
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.081
I like babies, but twins three times is too much!

50
00:02:43.781 --> 00:02:46.001
I got so tired carrying them around.

51
00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:49.662
I lived with the Hammonds for two years, and then Mr.

52
00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.463
Hammond died.

53
00:02:51.043 --> 00:02:55.084
I had to go to the orphanage because the Hammonds didn't want me any longer either.

54
00:02:55.784 --> 00:02:57.485
It was too crowded in their house."

55
00:02:58.226 --> 00:02:59.387
"Did you ever go to school?"

56
00:02:59.827 --> 00:03:00.627
Marilla asked.

57
00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:03.309
"A little bit," answered Anne.

58
00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:06.431
"I can read well, and I know lots of poetry!

59
00:03:06.992 --> 00:03:08.473
Don't you just love poetry?"

60
00:03:08.493 --> 00:03:10.314
"Were those women, Mrs.

61
00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:11.395
Thomas and Mrs.

62
00:03:11.475 --> 00:03:12.896
Hammond, good to you?"

63
00:03:13.296 --> 00:03:15.457
asked Marilla, looking at Anne carefully.

64
00:03:15.477 --> 00:03:20.941
"Uh um stammered Anne, blushing with embarrassment.

65
00:03:20.961 --> 00:03:23.102
"They tried to be good to me.

66
00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.184
I'm sure they meant to be good."

67
00:03:25.948 --> 00:03:27.869
Marilla asked no more questions.

68
00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:33.152
She suddenly felt pity for Anne, who hadn't had much love in her short life.

69
00:03:33.932 --> 00:03:35.233
Soon they arrived at Mrs.

70
00:03:35.273 --> 00:03:36.054
Spencer's house.

71
00:03:36.074 --> 00:03:38.175
"Well," Mrs.

72
00:03:38.215 --> 00:03:41.496
Spencer exclaimed, "you're the last folks I expected!

73
00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:43.177
How are you, Anne?"

74
00:03:43.197 --> 00:03:46.319
"All right," said Anne without smiling.

75
00:03:46.339 --> 00:03:49.561
"Mrs. Spencer," began Marilla.

76
00:03:49.581 --> 00:03:52.262
"I'm sorry, but there's been a mistake.

77
00:03:52.923 --> 00:03:55.224
We told the orphanage we wanted a boy."

78
00:03:56.496 --> 00:03:57.436
"Oh!" Mrs.

79
00:03:57.476 --> 00:03:58.217
Spencer said.

80
00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.097
"That's too bad.

81
00:04:00.777 --> 00:04:01.697
I'm very sorry."

82
00:04:01.718 --> 00:04:04.598
"I'm sorry too," said Marilla.

83
00:04:04.618 --> 00:04:06.559
"Can we send the child back?

84
00:04:07.259 --> 00:04:09.260
The orphanage will take her, won't they?"

85
00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.100
"I suppose so," said Mrs.

86
00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.181
Spencer thoughtfully.

87
00:04:13.201 --> 00:04:14.681
"But wait a minute.

88
00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.962
Mrs. Blewett was here yesterday.

89
00:04:17.662 --> 00:04:19.462
She told me she would like a little girl.

90
00:04:20.502 --> 00:04:23.003
Marilla was not very pleased to hear this.

91
00:04:23.703 --> 00:04:28.285
Mrs. Blewett had a terrible temper and did not treat servant girls well.

92
00:04:28.305 --> 00:04:30.185
"Look, there's Mrs.

93
00:04:30.225 --> 00:04:30.865
Blewett now!"

94
00:04:31.345 --> 00:04:31.906
said Mrs.

95
00:04:31.946 --> 00:04:36.247
Spencer. A thin-faced, frowning woman came over to the house.

96
00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:37.887
"How lucky!

97
00:04:38.627 --> 00:04:39.888
She can take Anne now!"

98
00:04:40.688 --> 00:04:42.989
Mrs. Spencer explained the mistake to Mrs.

99
00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.809
Blewett. Mrs.

100
00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:47.170
Blewett looked Anne over from head to toe.

101
00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.650
"How old are you and what's your name?"

102
00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:50.731
she demanded.

103
00:04:50.751 --> 00:04:55.552
"My name is Anne Shirley, and I'm eleven years old," Anne replied.

104
00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:59.471
"You're too thin, but you're wiry," snapped Mrs.

105
00:04:59.511 --> 00:05:01.973
Blewett. "The wiry ones are the best.

106
00:05:02.533 --> 00:05:04.355
You'll be a good girl and work hard.

107
00:05:05.155 --> 00:05:07.798
All right, Miss Cuthbert," she said to Marilla.

108
00:05:07.818 --> 00:05:09.519
"I'll take her home now."

109
00:05:11.621 --> 00:05:14.503
"I don't know," Marilla said slowly.

110
00:05:14.523 --> 00:05:18.286
"Matthew and I haven't decided what to do yet.

111
00:05:19.107 --> 00:05:23.270
If we decide not to keep Anne, I'll send her over tomorrow."

112
00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:26.108
"All right," said Mrs.

113
00:05:26.168 --> 00:05:27.549
Blewett ungraciously.

114
00:05:28.349 --> 00:05:32.011
At Marilla's words Anne's eyes grew bright like stars.

115
00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.892
"Can I really stay at Green Gables?"

116
00:05:35.472 --> 00:05:36.693
she whispered to Marilla.

117
00:05:36.713 --> 00:05:41.255
"We'll decide tonight," said Marilla crossly.

118
00:05:41.275 --> 00:05:42.655
"But you heard me.

119
00:05:43.356 --> 00:05:44.316
You might go to Mrs.

120
00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:47.377
Blewett. She needs you more than Matthew and I do."

121
00:05:47.397 --> 00:05:50.118
"Oh, send me to the orphanage instead!

122
00:05:50.779 --> 00:05:52.719
Mrs. Blewett looks like a monster!"

123
00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:53.760
said Anne.

124
00:05:54.636 --> 00:05:55.457
"Anne Shirley!

125
00:05:56.137 --> 00:05:57.198
Don't talk like that!"

126
00:05:57.638 --> 00:05:58.578
Marilla scolded.

127
00:05:58.598 --> 00:06:01.960
"Go and sit quietly and be a good girl!"

128
00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:06.383
"I'll be anything you want, if you will keep me," pleaded Anne.

129
00:06:07.063 --> 00:06:11.405
Later Marilla told Matthew about Anne's history and the trip to Mrs.

130
00:06:11.445 --> 00:06:12.246
Spencer's house.

131
00:06:13.086 --> 00:06:14.547
"I wouldn't give a dog to Mrs.

132
00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:16.148
Blewett!" said Matthew.

133
00:06:16.168 --> 00:06:17.649
"I don't like Mrs.

134
00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:24.597
Blewett's style either," admitted Marilla, "Since you want to keep the girl, I suppose she can stay.

135
00:06:25.397 --> 00:06:28.159
I've never brought up a child, especially a girl.

136
00:06:28.819 --> 00:06:32.221
I'll probably make a mess of it, but I'll do my best."

137
00:06:33.242 --> 00:06:35.584
Matthew's shy face glowed with delight.

138
00:06:35.604 --> 00:06:38.205
"Marilla, I hoped you would change your mind.

139
00:06:38.986 --> 00:06:40.446
She's such an interesting little thing."

140
00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:44.869
"Yes, well, don't interfere, Matthew," Marilla said.

141
00:06:44.889 --> 00:06:49.332
"I won't tell Anne tonight because she'll be so excited she won't sleep.

142
00:06:50.088 --> 00:06:55.579
An old maid might not know much about raising children, but neither does an old bachelor!

143
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.663
Goodness knows what will come of it!"
